# P4a for pclm10: the window server's touch-to-panel latency, with nobody at the phone.
# The software path reaches SpringBoard at about 136 s of kernel time, stays near 47 C in a 150 s run;
# home first (page 1 has Settings at 0.615/0.71), 40 s to settle, then two zigzags for tools/latency.py
# to fit against the screen recording.
/redwood/bin/hello_dyn started by launchd
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 130
/redwood/bin/rwtouch button home 200
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 3
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.615 0.71
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 40
/redwood/bin/rwtouch swipe 0.5 0.8 0.5 0.55 600
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 3
/redwood/bin/rwtouch zigzag 0.5 0.75 0.5 300 6
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 2
/redwood/bin/rwtouch zigzag 0.5 0.75 0.5 300 6
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 2
/redwood/bin/rwtouch button home 200
